Dear Sir or Madam,

I attach Day 3 of a serialised public record relating to BV20D01752 / CA-20=
24-001342 / AC-2025-LON-004293 / BL-2024-001217. The document, Orders Made W=
ithout Participation of a Disabled Litigant, addresses a single procedural q=
uestion: by what mechanism, and on what authority, were the statutory partic=
ipation measures the Court itself had ordered for a disabled litigant under =
FPR Part 3A withdrawn on 7 March 2024, without an order, a hearing, reasons,=
 or notification =E2=80=94 and why are the orders made since then procedurally uns=
afe.

Day 2 of this serialised public record, distributed on 1 May 2026, establis=
hed the suppression of disability evidence in the judgment record. This stat=
ement addresses the procedural consequence of that omission. The accompanyin=
g NHS clinical letter from Dr Omar Shoukry of the Central and North West Lon=
don NHS Foundation Trust, dated 17 April 2026, is contemporaneous evidence t=
hat the conditions the original participation directions were intended to ac=
commodate continue to require those adjustments. The accompanying Five Matte=
rs for Determination document of 20 April 2026 is the procedural anchor iden=
tifying the matters formally raised through court, parliamentary, and crimin=
al-referral channels for which no judicial determination has been identified=
. The accompanying Accountability Map of 1 May 2026 identifies every individ=
ual and institution placed on actual notice of this record.

Also attached is a one-page document, Public Record =E2=80=94 Days 1 to 7 =E2=80=94 Cor=
respondence with Pleaded Grounds of Judicial Review, setting out where this =
and the other public-record statements sit within the structure of the live =
judicial review (AC-2025-LON-004293). The five grounds advanced in the Amend=
ed Grounds of Claim of 2 January 2026 are reproduced verbatim. No judicial d=
etermination has been identified addressing those grounds.

The further days of this serialised public record will follow.

=20

Yours faithfully,

=20

Nadia Zahmoul

Litigant in Person

nadia@rosekross.com

